Previously, we learned how Promises rescued us from "Callback Hell." While a big improvement, chaining multiple `.then()` blocks for sequential asynchronous tasks can still become cumbersome.

The Problem with `.then()` Chains:

```javascript
fetch('https://api.example.com/data')
    .then(response => {
        return response.json();
    })
    .then(data => {
        console.log(data);
    })
    .catch(error => {
